        "department": null,
        "description": "This course introduces students to CMOS circuits, develops first-order current-voltage and capacitance-voltage models for transistors, transfer characteristics of CMOS inverter, performance estimation for circuits through logical effort, interconnects, combinational circuit design, circuit families, sequential circuit design including clocking and latching techniques, design of datapath subsystems (adders, shifters, multipliers etc.), design of memory subsystems. A course project using state-of-the-art computer aided design (CAD) tools in VLSI gives students hands-on exposer to the most current technology/process.",
